(a) Each holder of an operating license issued under this part for a nuclear power plant, and each applicant for such a license, shall establish and maintain an environmental qualification (EQ) program for electric equipment important to safety that is located in a harsh environment, as defined in paragraph (b) of this section. The EQ program must demonstrate that the electric equipment is qualified to perform its safety functions under postulated environmental conditions, including those that may result from accident conditions, throughout the installed life of the equipment. The program must include the following elements:

(1) Identification of electric equipment important to safety that is located in a harsh environment;
(2) Documentation of the qualification of the identified equipment, including the qualification method, test results, analyses, and other relevant information;
(3) Maintenance of the qualified status of the equipment throughout its installed life by ensuring that replacement equipment is qualified, that qualified life is not exceeded, and that any significant aging effects are managed;
(4) Procedures for the control of design changes, modifications, and repairs to ensure continued qualification; and
(5) Records sufficient to demonstrate compliance with the requirements of this section.

(b) For the purposes of this section, a 'harsh environment' means an environment that could result from a design basis event, including loss-of-coolant accidents, high-energy line breaks, or other events that could subject equipment to temperature, pressure, humidity, radiation, or chemical conditions beyond those expected during normal operation.

